[38;5;231m[49m⏺[39m Using hyperpowers:using-hyperpowers — this lands on rung 1 of the ladder.

  Dropping [38;5;153mnotes[39m destroys whatever data is in that column, and a Postgres/SQLite [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m is not reversible by a
  down-migration: rolling back can re-add the column, but the contents are gone permanently. "We stopped using it" is
  the claim I need confirmed before I write the migration — not permission by itself. Once the migration runs in
  production, any user-entered notes are unrecoverable except from backups.

  So before I touch anything:

